  "note": "Phase 6C \u2014 skip the full-history bf16 K/V backing pool by default. Kernel verification (vllm-flash-attn-dev flash_fwd_kernel.h L962-985/L1073-1100) confirmed the int4_packed template never reads bf16_k_batch / bf16_v_batch; both were dead memory + per-decode-step bandwidth. PHASE6C_BF16_BACKING_SKIP=1 (default) allocates a (1,1,H,D) stub and broadcasts to the kernel's expected shape via stride-0 expand. PHASE6C_BF16_BACKING_SKIP=0 reverts to legacy. Only phase5b_4c_paged_writer.py changed.",
